                <p>After “subsection 16(1)”, insert “or (1A)”.</p>
              </content>
            </hcontainer>
            <hcontainer name="item" eId="schedule-1__amdact-3__item-9">
              <num>22</num>
              <heading>Application of amendments</heading>
              <subsection eId="schedule-1__amdact-3__item-9__subsec-1">
                <num>1</num>
                <content>
                  <p>(1)	The amendments of <ref href="#sec-12">section 12</ref> of the <i>Australian Passports Act 2005</i> made by this Schedule apply to refusal/cancellation requests made in relation to a person after the commencement of this Schedule, whether the person became a reportable offender (within the meaning of that section) before or after that commencement.</p>
                </content>
              </subsection>
              <subsection eId="schedule-1__amdact-3__item-9__subsec-2">
                <num>2</num>
                <content>
                  <p>(2)	Section 22AA of the <i>Australian Passports Act 2005</i>, as inserted by this Schedule, applies to the cancellation of an Australian passport after the commencement of this Schedule, whether:</p>
                </content>
                <paragraph eId="schedule-1__amdact-3__item-9__subsec-2__para-a">
                  <num>a</num>
                  <content>
                    <p>the Australian passport was issued to a person before or after that commencement; or</p>
                  </content>
                </paragraph>
                <paragraph eId="schedule-1__amdact-3__item-9__subsec-2__para-b">
                  <num>b</num>
                  <content>
                    <p>the person became a reportable offender (<ref href="#sec-12">within the meaning of section 12</ref> of that Act) before or after that commencement.</p>
                  </content>
                </paragraph>
              </subsection>
              <subsection eId="schedule-1__amdact-3__item-9__subsec-3">
                <num>3</num>
                <content>
                  <p>(3)	Section 271A.1 of the <i>Criminal Code Act 199</i>5, as inserted by this Schedule, applies in relation to conduct engaged in by a person after the commencement of this Schedule, whether the person’s name is entered on a child protection offender register (however described) of a State or Territory before or after that commencement.</p>
                </content>
              </subsection>
              <subsection eId="schedule-1__amdact-3__item-9__subsec-4">
                <num>4</num>
                <content>
                  <p>(4)	The amendments of <ref href="#sec-13">section 13</ref> of the <i>Foreign Passports (Law Enforcement and Security) Act 2005</i> made by this Schedule apply to requests made in relation to a person after the commencement of this Schedule, whether the person became a reportable offender (within the meaning of that section) before or after that commencement.</p>
                </content>
              </subsection>
              <subsection eId="schedule-1__amdact-3__item-9__subsec-5">
                <num>5</num>
                <content>
                  <p>(5)	The amendments of <ref href="#sec-16">section 16</ref> of the <i>Foreign Passports (Law Enforcement and Security) Act 2005</i> made by this Schedule apply to an order for the surrender of a person’s foreign travel documents made after the commencement of this Schedule, whether:</p>
                </content>
                <paragraph eId="schedule-1__amdact-3__item-9__subsec-5__para-a">
                  <num>a</num>
                  <content>
                    <p>the foreign travel documents were issued to the person before or after that commencement; or</p>
                  </content>
                </paragraph>
                <paragraph eId="schedule-1__amdact-3__item-9__subsec-5__para-b">
                  <num>b</num>
                  <content>
                    <p>the person became a reportable offender (<ref href="#sec-13">within the meaning of section 13</ref> of that Act) before or after that commencement.</p>
                  </content>
                  <content>
                    <p>[<i>Minister’s second reading speech made in—</i></p>
                    <p><i>House of Representatives on 14 June 2017</i></p>
                    <p><i>Senate on 20 June 2017</i>]</p>
                    <p>(127/17)</p>
                  </content>
                </paragraph>
              </subsection>
